From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 23:36:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mb/lenovo/m720q_m920q: Wake on LAN after a shutdown, as the
 OEM does

The OEM firmware has Intel's "Wake on LAN Enable" on by default, the
override of the PCH that takes the wake of the LAN from S4 and S5
(WOL_EN_OVRD). coreboot leaves it off: the GbE device has its wake up
to S4 in the ACPI tables, so Linux does not arm it for S5, and a
shut-down M920x does not wake on LAN. On the machine running this
tree, GEN_PMCON_B reads 0x00060210, without the override.

Turn it on in the devicetree and offer the "wake_on_lan" option in
Energy Saver > Power, on by default.

TEST=Built lenovo/m920x: WolEnableOverride is true in static.c. The
wake itself is for the hardware test: shut down, then a magic packet
to the MAC address of the port.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/cfr.c         | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/devicetree.cb |  3 +++
 2 files changed, 19 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/cfr.c b/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/cfr.c
index 7db7c87419..6ae81352d1 100644
--- a/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/cfr.c
+++ b/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/cfr.c
@@ -322,10 +322,26 @@ static const struct sm_object energy_processor = SM_DECLARE_FORM({
 	},
 });
 
+/* Read by FSP-S parameters (soc/intel/cannonlake/fsp_params.c) */
+static const struct sm_object wake_on_lan = SM_DECLARE_BOOL({
+	.opt_name	= "wake_on_lan",
+	.ui_name	= "Wake on LAN from off",
+	.ui_helptext	= "Turn the computer on when a Wake-on-LAN packet comes to\n"
+			  "the Ethernet port after a shutdown (S5), as the OEM\n"
+			  "firmware does: the ACPI tables give the wake of the LAN up\n"
+			  "to S4, so the OS does not arm it for S5, and the PCH takes\n"
+			  "it anyway. The OS still arms the port itself (ethtool:\n"
+			  "Wake-on g).\n"
+			  "Default: on. Off: no wake on LAN after a shutdown; from\n"
+			  "sleep and hibernation the OS decides.",
+	.default_value	= true,
+});
+
 static const struct sm_object energy_power = SM_DECLARE_FORM({
 	.ui_name	= "Power",
 	.obj_list	= (const struct sm_object *[]) {
 		&power_on_after_fail,
+		&wake_on_lan,
 		NULL
 	},
 });
diff --git a/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/devicetree.cb b/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/devicetree.cb
index 2bc9c1a97e..59efe115a1 100644
--- a/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/devicetree.cb
+++ b/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/devicetree.cb
@@ -8,6 +8,9 @@ chip soc/intel/cannonlake
 	# Enhanced Intel SpeedStep, as the OEM firmware: P-states for the OS
 	register "eist_enable" = "true"
 
+	# Wake on LAN from S4 and S5, as the OEM firmware (the "wake_on_lan" option)
+	register "WolEnableOverride" = "true"
+
 	# Unmap unused CLKREQ lines, otherwise CLKSRC #0 won't work
 	register "PcieClkSrcClkReq[1]"	= "PCIE_CLK_NOTUSED"
 	register "PcieClkSrcClkReq[5]"	= "PCIE_CLK_NOTUSED"
-- 
2.47.3

